 devraient toujours être à ce niveau !","test":false,"importance":false,"trainingType":"EF","trainingCategory":"road_basic_endurance","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"EF_45","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"EF","value":327,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":45,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":false}]}],"difficulty":1,"trainingIndex":4,"weekDate":1788739200000,"status":"todo","stats":{"_t":"SessionExpectedStats","expectedDistance":7.894736842105263,"expectedDuration":2700},"paceZones":[{"kind":"Z2","duration":2700,"pace":{"value":327}}]},{"_t":"SmartSessionWithStats","sport":"road","name":"Affutage_10_600_S3_ HARD2","description":"Séance d'allure spécifique 10 km avec **3 intervalles de 5'** à ton allure 10 km entrecoupés de 3' de récupération.","displayName":"Allure 10 km","coachAdvice":"Une dernière séance à allure 10 km, qui n'est pas très difficile. À ce stade, l'entraînement est terminé : on n'est plus dans une logique de progression, mais plutôt d'entretien de la forme.\nMême si tu te sens bien, ne cours pas plus vite que ton allure prévue. Essaie plutôt de te relâcher et de courir de manière économique, en pensant au jour J et à la fin de course, où tu auras besoin de toute l'énergie économisée au début.","test":false,"importance":false,"trainingType":"Intensity","trainingCategory":"road_intensity","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"WU_20","exerciseType":"warm-up","pace":{"name":"EF","value":327,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":20,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":true}],"blockType":"warm-up"},{"repeat":3,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"A10_5","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"10km","value":247,"kind":"single-value","zoneKind":"Z4","abstract":false,"slug":"10km"},"durations":[{"value":5,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":false},{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":